# Line-ending policy: SQLx embeds `migrations/*.sql` at compile time
# byte-for-byte via `sqlx::migrate!`, and the schema-history table records
# SHA-384 checksums of that exact byte sequence. A `--autocrlf=true` host
# (Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which silently mutates
# the embedded checksum and the binary fails to start with
# `migration N was previously applied but has been modified`.
#
# Forcing `eol=lf` here keeps the working tree, the git blob, and the bytes
# embedded into every daemon binary identical on every host.
migrations/*.sql	text eol=lf

# Treat the rest of the SQL we ship as text the same way so future schema
# migrations never trip the same wire.
**/*.sql	text eol=lf
